Added 2026-09-12 for #57 (list and inspect Workflow Bundles in the TUI). Both
screens render the read-only `bundle-catalog` Projection through the Projection
Port; no OpenCode source crosses for them. What was taken and changed:

  bundle-list.tsx (from dialog-select.tsx; replaced by bundle-catalog.tsx in #190):
    Taken:   the selection model (one active index moved by the arrow keys,
             Return opens the active row) and the active-row highlight
             (background + bold).
    Changed: OpenCode glyph-marks only the *current* value; here the *focused*
             row carries a leading "› " glyph as well as the highlight, so focus
             reads without colour (ADR 0024 / #19). Movement clamps at the ends
             rather than wrapping. OpenCode's fuzzy-filter/group/flat option
             store collapses to the single Projection-driven list. The empty
             state names the headless install commands. #190 amends the original
             entry: the selection now drives the persistent inspector, substring
             search stays local to the Projection snapshot, movement still
             clamps rather than wraps, and scroll is now supplied by the vendored
             helper above.

  bundle-inspect.tsx (from diff-viewer.tsx; replaced by bundle-catalog.tsx and its
  private bundle-catalog-inspector.tsx submodule in #190):
    Taken:   a full-size route box and Escape = navigate back to the screen you
             came from (here restoring the list's selected row).
    Changed: #190 replaces the full-size route with the persistent inspector,
             split into bundle-catalog-inspector.tsx as the pure fact/routing
             renderer under bundle-catalog.tsx's Projection/focus controller.
             The copied PanelGroup/Panel subset supplies the two-pane/stacked
             layout, and the copied scroll helper drives the inspector's pinned
             OpenTUI scrollbox with explicit end clamping.

