Added 2026-09-19 for the thin npm launcher (#152). `bin/secant.mjs` is a
standalone Node launcher; no OpenCode source crosses (it lives outside
src/tui/vendor/ and is authored fresh). What was studied and changed:

  bin/secant.mjs (studied against packages/opencode/bin/opencode):
    Taken:   the signal-forwarding and exit-status shape — forward SIGINT/SIGTERM/
             SIGHUP to the spawned child, and on the child's exit re-raise its death
             signal on this process or exit with its code.
    Changed: resolution is Secant's own script-free, resolve-in-place design —
             OpenCode's postinstall binary-copy (the `.opencode` cache and the
             error-shim `.exe`) is deliberately rejected (spec #137). The launcher
             reads a pack-time-generated host-key map and resolves the matching
             per-platform package via `createRequire` from its canonicalized path
             (so pnpm layouts work), never downloading or copying a binary, and
             fails before spawn with distinct unsupported-target and
             missing-optional-package diagnostics.

